(5108010, 740519, 27482, '<td valign="top">Gave it a 6, two things that kept me from going higher as I really like the lighting/texture on the buildings.  Why did you include the lightpost there, it´s sticking out like a sore thumb?  Secondly, the pink hue on the clouds draws my eye there, I would have wanted to see it with the sepia toning everywhere.</td>', 'Gave it a 6, two things that kept me from going higher as I really like the lighting/texture on the buildings.  Why did you include the lightpost there, it´s sticking out like a sore thumb?  Secondly, the pink hue on the clouds draws my eye there, I would have wanted to see it with the sepia toning everywhere.', '2008-12-05 06:13:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5108012, 740809, 27482, '<td valign="top">Hehe, great expression :)</td>', 'Hehe, great expression :)', '2008-12-05 06:14:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5108015, 737065, 27482, '<td valign="top">I once heard a useful tip when it comes to b/w processing.  You should always consider converting to b/w when the colors in a shot were not interesting at all but here I get the feeling they were and I can´t help but wonder what this shot would have looked like in color, is it really more interesting b/w?</td>', 'I once heard a useful tip when it comes to b/w processing.  You should always consider converting to b/w when the colors in a shot were not interesting at all but here I get the feeling they were and I can´t help but wonder what this shot would have looked like in color, is it really more interesting b/w?', '2008-12-05 06:20:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5108019, 743453, 27482, '<td valign="top">Sorry but the color treatment in this shot is, pardon me for saying so, horrible.  The green looks awfully "neon" like and not natural at all.  Usually when I color something in post processing, I use a seperate layer for that, go nuts like you did here and then bring the opacity down on that layer to mute the effects, it usually comes out much better.  Put a 3 on it and at least thought I´d tell you why.</td>', 'Sorry but the color treatment in this shot is, pardon me for saying so, horrible.  The green looks awfully "neon" like and not natural at all.  Usually when I color something in post processing, I use a seperate layer for that, go nuts like you did here and then bring the opacity down on that layer to mute the effects, it usually comes out much better.  Put a 3 on it and at least thought I´d tell you why.', '2008-12-05 06:23:31.000000', NULL, 1),
