(5116273, 738999, 60614, '<td valign="top">I actually like both versions and don''t have a problem with the one that is processed.  Thanks for sharing.  I always like to see what you do to make your photos pop.  Congratulations on your finish.</td>', 'I actually like both versions and don''t have a problem with the one that is processed.  Thanks for sharing.  I always like to see what you do to make your photos pop.  Congratulations on your finish.', '2008-12-08 06:01:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116283, 743180, 33535, '<td valign="top">dude, you''re one of my hero''s on this site!<br/>this is a great shot indeed, reminded me of some movie with johnny depp in it. or was it leonardo di caprio...;)<br/>oh and i like the border, just so you know!</td>', 'dude, you''re one of my hero''s on this site!this is a great shot indeed, reminded me of some movie with johnny depp in it. or was it leonardo di caprio...;)oh and i like the border, just so you know!', '2008-12-08 06:05:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116284, 743325, 60614, '<td valign="top">Your photo is perfect just as is but the story <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97166" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">K10DGuy</a> left is icing on the cake.  Glad to see that it stayed in the 5''s instead of the 4''s.</td>', 'Your photo is perfect just as is but the story  K10DGuy left is icing on the cake.  Glad to see that it stayed in the 5''s instead of the 4''s.', '2008-12-08 06:05:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116294, 743773, 33535, '<td valign="top">this shot suffers from the heavvy processing, but otherwise it''s darn great!</td>', 'this shot suffers from the heavvy processing, but otherwise it''s darn great!', '2008-12-08 06:10:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116308, 743284, 47852, '<td valign="top">I have to say, I''m happy to see that this got the posthumous blue!  Such a whimsical shot that oozes happy, warm fuzzy feelings!  The lens flare looks like little bits of magic sprinkling down over the couple.  Wonderful! :)</td>', 'I have to say, I''m happy to see that this got the posthumous blue!  Such a whimsical shot that oozes happy, warm fuzzy feelings!  The lens flare looks like little bits of magic sprinkling down over the couple.  Wonderful! :)', '2008-12-08 06:19:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116311, 743658, 67152, '<td valign="top">Paul - A nice Christmas card shot - I wonder if a slightly different composition would have helped here.  I think the tree in the background is good to provide some color and contrast, but it seems to unbalance the image.  In addition, the whites seem a bit bright on the screen - it probably will look great printed out</td>', 'Paul - A nice Christmas card shot - I wonder if a slightly different composition would have helped here.  I think the tree in the background is good to provide some color and contrast, but it seems to unbalance the image.  In addition, the whites seem a bit bright on the screen - it probably will look great printed out', '2008-12-08 06:23:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116312, 743423, 47852, '<td valign="top">Glad to see this one getting the posthumous yellow!  A beautiful, abstract photo that captures a fleeting natural moment.  Wonderful! :)</td>', 'Glad to see this one getting the posthumous yellow!  A beautiful, abstract photo that captures a fleeting natural moment.  Wonderful! :)', '2008-12-08 06:24:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116314, 740085, 67152, '<td valign="top">Rich - nice simple composition.  The sky is very cool with the streams of light.  I just wonder about the processing - it seems tonemapped as there are some significant halos around the grass umbrella.</td>', 'Rich - nice simple composition.  The sky is very cool with the streams of light.  I just wonder about the processing - it seems tonemapped as there are some significant halos around the grass umbrella.', '2008-12-08 06:27:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116315, 741996, 67152, '<td valign="top">the lines created by the bridge and shadows really give this a dizzy-ing feel - and i think that works pretty well for it</td>', 'the lines created by the bridge and shadows really give this a dizzy-ing feel - and i think that works pretty well for it', '2008-12-08 06:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116316, 738603, 61012, '<td valign="top">Congratulation Peter. Awesome shot!</td>', 'Congratulation Peter. Awesome shot!', '2008-12-08 06:29:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116317, 738603, 47906, '<td valign="top">Hey Peter, Congrats on the Blue. I thought I recognized this beauty from VINS but wasnt totally sure enough to leave a comment as I am sure there are others out there. Truely a remarkable image. Congrats once again.</td>', 'Hey Peter, Congrats on the Blue. I thought I recognized this beauty from VINS but wasnt totally sure enough to leave a comment as I am sure there are others out there. Truely a remarkable image. Congrats once again.', '2008-12-08 06:29:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116333, 738999, 37730, '<td valign="top">fantastic :)</td>', 'fantastic :)', '2008-12-08 06:47:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116337, 738999, 18655, '<td valign="top">Way to go Roz - very well deserved!!<br/> <br/>I also like both versions. The added processing brings the details out. You can see that it is processed quite a bit but the added detail is interesting. I also see that you used f/10 which brings the best out of the EF100mm macro lens (peak performance is in fact f/11).<br/> <br/>I''m very interested in which lens set-up and what type of flash you used though (twin flash?). I know that the image details say 100mm 2.8 macro. BUT... the uncropped image shows that your lens is able to fill the frame with approx 3/8" of focused subject (roughly 1/8" bug plus space). With the 100mm macro lens I can only manage 1". With an added 68mm of extension tubes (the entire Kenko kit), the frame can focus on 3/8". I assume this is what you did but I''m not not sure.<br/> <br/>I like "extreme" macro photography a lot and see from your portfolio that you are one of the masters on the site. So I am very curious how you do it and what you used in addition to the 100mm. Maybe a "How''d They do That" on the matter would have been interesting for a few of the members - at least for me! :)<br/> <br/>In any case; an excellent job!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-08 14:05:38.</i></td>', 'Way to go Roz - very well deserved!! I also like both versions. The added processing brings the details out. You can see that it is processed quite a bit but the added detail is interesting. I also see that you used f/10 which brings the best out of the EF100mm macro lens (peak performance is in fact f/11). I''m very interested in which lens set-up and what type of flash you used though (twin flash?). I know that the image details say 100mm 2.8 macro. BUT... the uncropped image shows that your lens is able to fill the frame with approx 3/8" of focused subject (roughly 1/8" bug plus space). With the 100mm macro lens I can only manage 1". With an added 68mm of extension tubes (the entire Kenko kit), the frame can focus on 3/8". I assume this is what you did but I''m not not sure. I like "extreme" macro photography a lot and see from your portfolio that you are one of the masters on the site. So I am very curious how you do it and what you used in addition to the 100mm. Maybe a "How''d They do That" on the matter would have been interesting for a few of the members - at least for me! :) In any case; an excellent job!', '2008-12-08 06:48:54.000000', '2008-12-08 14:05:38.000000', 0),
(5116339, 743343, 89341, '<td valign="top">Wow, so I was way off the mark! You have some great kit there to get a shot like this, I freely admit that it''s bizarre I thought something wasn''t right as it looked too good to be a real shot!! For what it''s worth I still gave you a 5! I''ve just looked through your profile and you have some great shots there.</td>', 'Wow, so I was way off the mark! You have some great kit there to get a shot like this, I freely admit that it''s bizarre I thought something wasn''t right as it looked too good to be a real shot!! For what it''s worth I still gave you a 5! I''ve just looked through your profile and you have some great shots there.', '2008-12-08 06:50:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5116344, 740999, 14603, '<td valign="top">Nothing short of brilliant.<br/>I especially like the processing, the lighting is superb.<br/>Good to see the voters have warmed to the "painterly look"..changed days<br/> <br/>Makes me want to get out there and find these shots.<br/> <br/>Congratulations Neil.</td>', 'Nothing short of brilliant.I especially like the processing, the lighting is superb.Good to see the voters have warmed to the "painterly look"..changed days Makes me want to get out there and find these shots. Congratulations Neil.', '2008-12-08 06:55:36.000000', NULL, 0),
