(5117706, 742182, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by boyd2000:</b></div><hr/><i> Care to enlighten those of us that are a little slow about the significance of the bridge Jason?  Is it the bridge to her growing up?  Wow, I can''t believe Sofia <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=91783" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">ScooterMcNutty </a>is a 15 year old!  She looks like a model.  She has really matured in the past couple of years and I''m sure has a great future ahead of her.  Kailey is pretty cool too.  Good job, but until I see an explanation my (and other peoples) comment below still stands.  ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>ok....are you guys ready? is everyone sitting down? have you put the kids to bed? here is the story:<b>THERE IS NO FREAKIN STORY!!!!</b> lol seriously we were out shooting in Tacoma and I just really like the underside of the bridge as a backdrop, i liked the randomness of someone all made up standing under a bridge in the inner city. when i was getting these comments during the voting i was thinking "man, if this was one of those bizarre ads in vogue magazine people would think the photographer was brilliant"<br/>As for the title, it was just the first thing that came to mind, basically just the two main elements in the shot, thats all :)</td>', 'Originally posted by boyd2000: Care to enlighten those of us that are a little slow about the significance of the bridge Jason?  Is it the bridge to her growing up?  Wow, I can''t believe Sofia  ScooterMcNutty is a 15 year old!  She looks like a model.  She has really matured in the past couple of years and I''m sure has a great future ahead of her.  Kailey is pretty cool too.  Good job, but until I see an explanation my (and other peoples) comment below still stands.  ;-)   ok....are you guys ready? is everyone sitting down? have you put the kids to bed? here is the story:THERE IS NO FREAKIN STORY!!!! lol seriously we were out shooting in Tacoma and I just really like the underside of the bridge as a backdrop, i liked the randomness of someone all made up standing under a bridge in the inner city. when i was getting these comments during the voting i was thinking "man, if this was one of those bizarre ads in vogue magazine people would think the photographer was brilliant"As for the title, it was just the first thing that came to mind, basically just the two main elements in the shot, thats all :)', '2008-12-08 16:52:31.000000', NULL, 0),
