(5119989, 738897, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pawdrix:</b></div><hr/><i> She''s awesome. I am now one with those 85mm lenses (1.4 or 1.8 Nikon/Canon). Unmistakeable. Gotta love''em.<br/> <br/>eta: An odd thing. You''re the only one on this site that I would hire specifically, to remove those darker circles under her eyes, if I needed an editor. Whassup wit dat? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks Steve.<br/>Wassup with the dark circles or the hiring part ;)<br/> <br/>Here is the original:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=746037" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/746037.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/746037.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/15000-19999/19708/120/746037.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I am trying really hard to not make my shots a PS creation, just natural enhancements.<br/>I am getting there as far as getting it right in-camera, all in manual mode, including flash.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by pawdrix: She''s awesome. I am now one with those 85mm lenses (1.4 or 1.8 Nikon/Canon). Unmistakeable. Gotta love''em. eta: An odd thing. You''re the only one on this site that I would hire specifically, to remove those darker circles under her eyes, if I needed an editor. Whassup wit dat?  Thanks Steve.Wassup with the dark circles or the hiring part ;) Here is the original:  I am trying really hard to not make my shots a PS creation, just natural enhancements.I am getting there as far as getting it right in-camera, all in manual mode, including flash. ', '2008-12-09 16:05:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5119990, 738897, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by chromeydome:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>luminous skin tone, excellent composition/pose, intriguing expression &amp; eye </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Woah - how cool is this??<br/>Thanks! This is as good or better than a fav!</td>', 'Originally posted by chromeydome: PostLuminous Award Nominee!luminous skin tone, excellent composition/pose, intriguing expression & eye  Woah - how cool is this??Thanks! This is as good or better than a fav!', '2008-12-09 16:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5119998, 738897, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Coley:</b></div><hr/><i> Here is a huge compliment ... I had this as a kiwiness entry and a high finish ... this is an awesome shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for what I consider an ultimate compliment on my image Cole.<br/>To be compared with Gary, well, what can I say but wow!<br/> <br/>And thanks to all that left such positive and complimentary words on this.</td>', 'Originally posted by Coley: Here is a huge compliment ... I had this as a kiwiness entry and a high finish ... this is an awesome shot!  Thanks for what I consider an ultimate compliment on my image Cole.To be compared with Gary, well, what can I say but wow! And thanks to all that left such positive and complimentary words on this.', '2008-12-09 16:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
